==============================================================================
 Real Test: Windows client -> server in WSL2
==============================================================================
Manual test record. Both sides run on one physical computer, but on two
operating systems with their own IP addresses, so the traffic crosses the
Hyper-V virtual network (vEthernet (WSL)) instead of loopback.

date        : 2026-11-12 16:13
server      : WSL2 Ubuntu, eth0 172.17.107.87, ./server -p 9090 -d 1
client      : Windows 11, 172.17.96.1, win_client.exe (tests/win_client.c, built with make win-client)
capture     : dumpcap -i "vEthernet (WSL (Hyper-V firewall))" -f "tcp port 9090" -> logs/real_test.pcapng

